\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {One account of all three failures: the frame is read backwards.} (\textbf  {a}) The same four numbers under the two readings, shaded by how good each cell is for the focal player, whose action indexes the rows. Under the stated objective the agent minimises a penalty, so the 0 is the prize; under a reward reading the 10 is. Every action the two readings prescribe is the inverse of the other, for both personas. (\textbf  {b}) The prediction at the opening move, where no history exists and the prompt is the only input. Agents told they are selfish open cooperatively far more often than agents told they are cooperative, in all four models, with 95\% bootstrap intervals resampling whole dyads. (\textbf  {c}) The prediction inside the memory-one fingerprint. State labels carry the penalty the focal agent received. All four cooperate readily after CD, where the agent has just collected the largest entry on the table and every canonical rule except AllC prescribes 0; three of four cooperate less after DC, where it collected nothing. Dashes mark tit-for-tat.}}{13}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:misread}{{4}{13}{\textbf {One account of all three failures: the frame is read backwards.} (\textbf {a}) The same four numbers under the two readings, shaded by how good each cell is for the focal player, whose action indexes the rows. Under the stated objective the agent minimises a penalty, so the 0 is the prize; under a reward reading the 10 is. Every action the two readings prescribe is the inverse of the other, for both personas. (\textbf {b}) The prediction at the opening move, where no history exists and the prompt is the only input. Agents told they are selfish open cooperatively far more often than agents told they are cooperative, in all four models, with 95\% bootstrap intervals resampling whole dyads. (\textbf {c}) The prediction inside the memory-one fingerprint. State labels carry the penalty the focal agent received. All four cooperate readily after CD, where the agent has just collected the largest entry on the table and every canonical rule except AllC prescribes 0; three of four cooperate less after DC, where it collected nothing. Dashes mark tit-for-tat}{figure.caption.11}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {3.5}One account of all three: the frame is misread}{13}{subsection.3.5}\protected@file@percent }
